  "limitations": [
    "Fixed ten-match historical batch, not sustained saturation, SMT or NUMA qualification.",
    "Three repetitions per variant on one host; min/max and paired ratios describe this experiment, not an uncertainty interval across machines or workloads.",
    "Isolated modules share one process and GC; RSS is not attributed per variant. Base.summarysize of snapshot/worker is retained graph size, not process RSS.",
    "Preparation and reset copies are included in campaign time. The first experiment includes per-frame refresh; the final closed static campaign skips it. Reset probes exclude one-time preparation.",
    "All variants slowed in the final repetition; order was balanced, but three repetitions do not isolate host drift. Paired combined/baseline speedups remain positive in all three rounds.",
    "Compact geometry versus prepared reset alone has mixed paired outcomes; its independent throughput benefit is not established.",
    "Prepared reset retains mutable Peg objects and rebuilds identity maps; this is not a full level-wide shared geometry/state rewrite.",
    "A small residual first-trial compilation cost, if present, is reported per trial."
